{"reference":"2 Chronicles 29","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":29,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Chapter Boundary to Notice","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter narrates Hezekiah’s reopening, cleansing, and renewal of worship at the house of Jehovah. Its sacrifice is offered “for all Israel,” which gives the restoration a wider horizon than Judah alone. The related Passover invitation and celebration belong to the continuing account rather than to the events narrated here; chapter 29 itself concludes with the temple service being set in order.","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 29:1-36"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_029_e490a84f5b3657d701ebeaed"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}